<body class="public legal">
{#- Four documents, one template. They share a head, a lockup and a foot, and the three
    hand-written copies of that foot are the reason this is not four files.

    design.md governs the product. It does not govern these: a privacy notice and terms
    of service are legal instruments and are drafted as such, in formal register with
    defined terms and numbered clauses a reader can cite. They still pass the brand
    tests unchanged — the name stays lowercase and nothing is exclaimed — because
    defining the Service in clause 1 means the name need not carry a formal sentence.

    Substance and structure adapted from 37signals' open-source policies under CC BY 4.0,
    credited at the foot as that licence requires. The privacy notice follows the order
    of GDPR Article 13; a notice omitting any of its items is not a notice. -#}
<main class="sheet">
  {#- One row on the sheet's own grid: the name at one corner, the door and the light
