  {% if which == 'privacy' %}
  <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
  <p class="lede">This Notice is given pursuant to Articles 13 and 14 of Regulation (EU)
    2016/679 (the "General Data Protection Regulation") and describes the processing of
    personal data carried out in connection with targum.</p>

  <h2>Identity of the Controller</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The controller of the personal data described in this Notice is David
      Langellotti (the "Controller"), who operates the service made available at
      targum.page (the "Service").</li>
    <li>The Controller may be contacted at
      <a href="mailto:hello@targum.page">hello@targum.page</a> in respect of any matter
      arising under this Notice, including the exercise of any right set out at clause 7
      below.</li>
    <li>The Controller has not appointed a data protection officer, no such appointment
      being required under Article 37.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>This Notice applies to personal data relating to persons who hold an account
      with the Service, who request access to it, or who otherwise access the pages
      made available at targum.page (each, a "Data Subject").</li>
    <li>This Notice does not apply to any website to which the Service links and over
      which the Controller exercises no control.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Categories of data, purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <p>The Controller processes only such personal data as is necessary for the purposes
    stated. The categories processed, the purpose of each and the legal basis relied
    upon are as follows.</p>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li><b>Electronic mail address.</b> Processed for the purposes of authenticating
      the Data Subject, maintaining the account and communicating with the Data Subject
      in relation to the Service. The Service employs no password; the address
      constitutes the account. Legal basis: Article 6(1)(b), performance of a contract
      to which the Data Subject is party.</li>
    <li><b>Material retained by the Data Subject.</b> Namely words and phrases marked
      by the Data Subject, together with any notes, meanings, documents opened, reading
      positions and dates of reading. Processed for the purpose of providing the Service.
      Legal basis: Article 6(1)(b).</li>
    <li><b>Material uploaded by the Data Subject.</b> Namely any file supplied by the
      Data Subject and any targum generated from it. Processed for the purpose of
      providing the Service. Legal basis: Article 6(1)(b).</li>
    <li><b>Records of requests for authentication links.</b> Namely the electronic mail
      address to which each such request relates and the time of the request, whether or
      not an account exists for that address. Processed for the purpose of enforcing a
      rate limit, without which the authentication form could be employed to transmit
      unsolicited mail to third parties from the Controller's domain. Legal basis:
      Article 6(1)(f), the legitimate interests of the Controller and of such third
      parties in preventing the misuse of the Service.</li>
    <li><b>Server access records.</b> Namely the internet protocol address from which a
      connection is made, the resource requested and the time of the request, recorded
      by the reverse proxy through which the Service is served. Authentication tokens
      are removed from each record before it is written. Processed for the purposes of
      diagnosing faults and detecting misuse. Legal basis: Article 6(1)(f).</li>
    <li>Where processing is founded upon Article 6(1)(f), the Data Subject may object
      to that processing in accordance with clause 7.6, and the Controller shall state
      which of the operations concerned it is able to cease without terminating the
      account.</li>
    <li>Authentication tokens and session identifiers are stored in the form of a
      one-way cryptographic digest and not in their original form.</li>
    <li>No processing is undertaken for the purposes of advertising, profiling or
      behavioural analytics. The Service transmits no analytics data, employs no
      third-party script, and sets no cookie other than that which maintains an
      authenticated session. A generated targum makes no network request whatsoever.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Recipients</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>Personal data is not sold, and is not disclosed to any person for that person's
      own marketing purposes.</li>
    <li>The Controller engages the following processors, each of which processes
      personal data only upon the Controller's instructions and for the purpose stated.
      <dl>
    <dt>Hetzner Online GmbH (Federal Republic of Germany)</dt>
    <dd>Provision of the server upon which the Service and its data reside.</dd>

    <dt>Resend, Inc. (United States of America)</dt>
    <dd>Transmission of authentication messages. Receives the electronic mail address of
      the Data Subject and the content of that message.</dd>

    <dt>Anthropic PBC (United States of America)</dt>
    <dd>Translation of text presented for reading. Receives that text and does not
      receive the electronic mail address of the Data Subject. Anthropic states that
      inputs and outputs are deleted within thirty days of receipt or generation and are
      not used to train models.</dd>
      </dl>
    </li>
    <li>Save as provided at clause 4.2, the Controller discloses personal data only
      where compelled to do so by law, or where disclosure is necessary to investigate
      use of the Service against another person.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Transfers to third countries</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The server upon which the Service operates is situated at Falkenstein in the
      Federal Republic of Germany.</li>
    <li>Two of the processors identified at clause 4.2 are established in the United
      States of America. Accordingly, the electronic mail address of the Data Subject
      and the text presented for translation are transferred to that third country.</li>
    <li>No other transfer of personal data outside the European Economic Area is
      undertaken.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>Personal data is retained for no longer than is necessary for the purposes for
      which it is processed.</li>
    <li>The period applicable to each category, or the criteria by which that period is
      determined, is set out in the
      <a href="/retention">Data Retention Schedule</a>, which forms part of this
      Notice.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Rights of the Data Subject</h2>
  <p>Subject to the conditions and exceptions provided by the General Data Protection
    Regulation, the Data Subject has the following rights.</p>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li><b>Access</b> (Article 15). To obtain confirmation as to whether personal data
      concerning the Data Subject is processed and, where it is, a copy of that data.
      This right may be exercised directly and without application by means of the
      function styled "Download your words" upon
      <a href="/you">the profile page</a>, which returns the entirety of the account in
      machine-readable form.</li>
    <li><b>Rectification</b> (Article 16). To obtain the correction of inaccurate
      personal data.</li>
    <li><b>Erasure</b> (Article 17). To obtain the deletion of personal data. The
      procedure is set out in the
      <a href="/deletion">Erasure and Account Closure Procedure</a>.</li>
    <li><b>Restriction of processing</b> (Article 18).</li>
    <li><b>Portability</b> (Article 20). To receive personal data in a structured,
      commonly used and machine-readable format, and to transmit it to another
      controller. The function identified at clause 7.1 satisfies this right.</li>
    <li><b>Objection</b> (Article 21). To object, on grounds relating to the Data
      Subject's particular situation, to processing founded upon Article 6(1)(f).</li>
    <li>Rights not exercisable by the means described above may be exercised by written
      application to <a href="mailto:hello@targum.page">hello@targum.page</a>. The
      Controller shall respond within one month of receipt, which period may be extended
      by two further months where necessary, the Data Subject being informed of any such
      extension.</li>
    <li>The Controller shall require that any such application be made from the
      electronic mail address recorded against the account, verification of identity
      being necessary in order that disclosure does not itself occasion the harm the
      right exists to prevent.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The Data Subject has the right under Article 77 to lodge a complaint with a
      supervisory authority, in particular in the Member State of the Data Subject's
      habitual residence, place of work or of the alleged infringement.</li>
    <li>The exercise of that right is without prejudice to any other administrative or
      judicial remedy.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Requirement to provide data</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The provision of an electronic mail address is a requirement necessary to enter
      into a contract for the Service. The Data Subject is under no obligation to
      provide it, but the Controller is unable to furnish an account in its absence.</li>
    <li>No decision producing legal effects concerning the Data Subject, or similarly
      significantly affecting the Data Subject, is taken on the basis of automated
      processing within the meaning of Article 22.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Amendment of this Notice</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The Controller may amend this Notice from time to time. The date of the last
      amendment appears below.</li>
    <li>The Service is developed in the open and the history of every amendment is
      publicly recorded.</li>
  </ol>

