  {% elif which == 'retention' %}
  <h1>Data Retention Schedule</h1>
  <p class="lede">This Schedule is given pursuant to Article 13(2)(a) of the General
    Data Protection Regulation and forms part of the
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. Each period stated is enforced by the
    software rather than by administrative practice.</p>

  <h2>Periods of retention</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li><b>Authentication link.</b> Twenty minutes from issue, and one use. A link
      presented a second time is refused and a further link must be requested.</li>
    <li><b>Authenticated session.</b> Ninety days from the date upon which the session
      was last used, whereupon it expires.</li>
    <li><b>Record of a request for an authentication link.</b> Retained for so long as
      is required to operate the rate limit described at clause 3.4 of the
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>, and no longer.</li>
    <li><b>A targum deleted by the User.</b> Seven days, during which period it is held
      in the trash, the number of days remaining is displayed and restoration is
      available. Upon expiry the directory and all material generated within it are
      deleted.</li>
    <li><b>An account closed by the User.</b> Seven days from the request for closure.
      Upon expiry the following are deleted: words, meanings, phrases, documents, dates
      of reading, sessions, authentication links and the account record itself, together
      with all files generated for the account.</li>
    <li><b>Material retained by the User.</b> Until deleted by the User or until closure
      of the account. No period of inactivity causes such material to be deleted.</li>
    <li><b>Server access records.</b> Written by the reverse proxy and rotated by file
      size, such that the records held comprise the recent past rather than the whole.
      Retained for so long as they remain of use in diagnosing faults and detecting
      misuse.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Qualifications</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>Deletion of expired material is performed upon restart of the Service.
      Accordingly a period of seven days stated above is to be construed as a period of
      not less than seven days.</li>
    <li>The database is copied nightly and the fourteen most recent copies are retained.
      An account deleted in accordance with clause 1.5 above may therefore persist
      within a backup for a further period not exceeding fourteen days. A copy
      transmitted from the server is encrypted before transmission. No backup is read
      save where restoration is required.</li>
    <li>Text transmitted to Anthropic PBC for translation is deleted by that processor
      in accordance with its own published policy, namely within thirty days of receipt.
      Deletion effected under this Schedule does not accelerate that period.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Erasure upon request</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The procedure by which a Data Subject may obtain erasure is set out in the
      <a href="/deletion">Erasure and Account Closure Procedure</a>.</li>
    <li>Enquiries concerning this Schedule may be addressed to
      <a href="mailto:hello@targum.page">hello@targum.page</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  {% else %}
  <h1>Erasure and Account Closure</h1>
  <p class="lede">This document sets out the procedure by which a User may obtain the
    deletion of an individual targum or the closure of an account, and the consequences
    of each. It gives effect to the right of erasure under Article 17 of the General
    Data Protection Regulation.</p>

  <h2>Export prior to closure</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>Before closing an account the User is advised to obtain a copy of its contents
      by means of the function styled "Download your words" upon
      <a href="/you">the profile page</a>, which returns the whole of the account,
      comprising every word, phrase, meaning and note, in machine-readable form.</li>
    <li>No copy is retained by the Operator for the User's benefit after the period
      specified at clause 2.3, and none can be furnished thereafter.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Closure of an account</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The function styled "Delete account" upon
      <a href="/you">the profile page</a> initiates closure. Confirmation is required
      before the request takes effect.</li>
    <li>Upon confirmation the User is signed out of every browser and the account ceases
      to function immediately.</li>
    <li>Seven days thereafter the account record and all data associated with it are
      deleted in accordance with clause 1.5 of the
      <a href="/retention">Data Retention Schedule</a>.</li>
    <li>No reason for closure is required and none is requested.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Withdrawal of a request for closure</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>A request for closure may be withdrawn at any time within the period specified
      at clause 2.3 by written application to
      <a href="mailto:hello@targum.page">hello@targum.page</a>.</li>
    <li>No function is provided within the Service for that purpose, the account having
      already been signed out of every browser.</li>
    <li>Upon expiry of that period the deletion is irreversible and cannot be
      effected in reverse by the Operator or by any other person.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Matters not reached by deletion</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>Backups retain the fourteen most recent nightly copies, and an account may
      persist within one of them for a further period not exceeding fourteen days.</li>
    <li>Server access records persist until rotated.</li>
    <li>Text transmitted for translation is deleted by Anthropic PBC within thirty days
      of receipt in accordance with its own policy.</li>
    <li>Each of the foregoing is stated in full in the
      <a href="/retention">Data Retention Schedule</a>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Deletion of an individual targum</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>The function styled "Delete" upon the corresponding row within the library
      deletes a single targum. The account is unaffected.</li>
    <li>The targum is held in the trash for seven days, during which period the number
      of days remaining is displayed and restoration is available by means of the
      function styled "Put back".</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Material published in error</h2>
  <ol class="clauses">
    <li>A person who considers that material available through the Service infringes a
      right of that person may give notice under clause 6.1 of the
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</li>
  </ol>
  {% endif %}

